<title>USA: N.Y. business loans fell $326 mln in July 9 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans fell $326 mln in July 9 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $326 million to $46,142 million in the week ended July 9, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $323 million to $46,417 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $1,499 million to $870,925 million.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
